
= Outreach
I take part in outreach events, directed mostly towards girls, to encourage them to overcome stereotypes and engage in long scientific studies, because science is awesome!

=== Mentoring
I have been mentoring high school girls to help them with their career choices and the world of science jobs since Aug 2020 (via Animaths).

=== Event organisation 
- *Young Women Mathematician and Computer Scientists Days (Inria Paris)*
\n During these two days, high school girls discover how to do research in mathematics by working on challenging open problem under supervision, attend talks by women scientists and meet women Ph.D. and post-docs, to discover possible futures in maths and computer science.
  -- *2020*: Designed, then fully organised and hosted the hybrid Inria Paris 2020 event, with the help of [https://www.di.ens.fr/eloise.berthier/index.html Eloise Berthier]. 
  -- *2019*: Co-organised the on site edition with [https://www.di.ens.fr/eloise.berthier/index.html Eloise Berthier] and [https://who.paris.inria.fr/Matthieu.Lequesne/index.php Matthieu Lequesne]. 

=== Speed meetings
- *2020: Girls and math: a luminous equation*
\nTook part in speed meetings between girls and researchers to talk about math and computer science careers. ([https://filles-et-maths.fr/journees-filles-et-maths/ Event description]) \n (05\/2020: Sorbonne, 08\/2020: Online)

- *2020: Engineers in the classroom (Lycée Jean Moulin)*
\nDescribed to high school students what the job of a software engineer is, as well as different interesting machine learning uses and ethical questions in daily life.

=== Programming introduction
- *2019: Highschool students summer school (ESPCI)*
\nIntroduced the different jobs of computer science engineer to high school girls, and animated an introductory software development workshop in Python over an afternoon. ([https://www.espci.fr/fr/actualites/2019/lyceennes-une-ecole-d-ete-juste-pour-vous Event description])

